Automated Vault Backup (Git Auto-Commit)
 * Trigger: Scheduled using a cron expression (e.g., every 6 hours) or triggered on push events to capture regular vault snapshots.
 * Action: Utilizes actions like git-auto-commit-action to automatically stage, commit, and push modified Markdown files and attachments back to your repository, serving as an extra layer of cloud redundancy.
Digital Garden & Quartz Publishing
 * Trigger: Configured to run on: [push] whenever updates are committed to your main branch.
 * Action: Automatically builds your Obsidian vault into a public-facing static site using static site generators like Quartz or the Digital Garden plugin, deploying the compiled HTML directly to GitHub Pages.
Markdown Linting and Link Validation
 * Trigger: Set to run on pull requests or scheduled weekly code/content checks.
 * Action: Executes markdownlint or custom scripts to check for broken internal wiki-links ([[link]]), uniform header spacing, and consistent frontmatter metadata across all notes.
Directory Structure and Permissions Setup
 * File Placement: Store individual pipeline definitions as YAML files (e.g., backup.yml, publish.yml) directly inside the .github/workflows/ directory.
 * Repository Permissions: Navigate to your GitHub repository Settings > Actions > General, scroll to Workflow permissions, and select Read and write permissions to allow automated scripts to push commits back to your repository.
